 ## Overview
-Light-SMAE is a smooth manifold auto-encoder that learns a low-dimensional, differentiable latent representation of high-dynamic-range (HDR) environment maps, serving as a strong regularizer or prior for inverse volume rendering and reflectance decomposition [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from direct optimization of lighting parameters by constraining the solution space to a smooth manifold learned from data, which enables stable gradient-based optimization of illumination in ill-posed inverse problems [S1, unofficial].
+Light-SMAE is a smooth manifold auto-encoder that learns a low-dimensional, differentiable latent representation of high-dynamic-range (HDR) environment maps, serving as a strong regularizer or prior for reflectance decomposition and inverse rendering [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from direct optimization of lighting parameters by constraining the solution space to a smooth manifold learned from data, which enables stable gradient-based optimization of illumination in ill-posed inverse problems [S1, unofficial].
 
